1. DEFINITIONS
   1.1 "Author": Yovani Torres Favier, owner of all rights.
   1.2 "Software": this entire repository and any prior or later
       version, including source and built code; architecture, folder
       structure, data flows, orchestrator, workers, functions and
       scripts; configuration, deployment and operations files; prompts,
       AI-agent instructions, skills and templates (including CLAUDE.md,
       AGENTS.md, SKILLS.md and ENCUESTAS.md); survey designs and data
       models; interface, visual design, styles, icons and images;
       documentation, comments and commit messages; and the full history.
   1.3 "Content": articles, text, audio, podcasts, video, images,
       surveys, results and any other material generated, published or
       served by the Software or yamacoa.com, whether authored directly
       or generated automatically.
   1.4 "Brand": the name "Yamacoa", the domain yamacoa.com, its logos,
       visual identity and any associated distinctive sign.
   1.5 "Derivative Work": any work based in whole or in part on the
       Software or Content, including modifications, adaptations,
       translations, ports to another language or framework,
       refactorings, reimplementations reproducing its structure or
       expressive logic, and combinations with other software.
   1.6 "Use": any copying, execution, deployment, distribution, public
       communication, transformation or exploitation, by any means.

2. OWNERSHIP
   The Software, Content and Brand belong exclusively to the Author,
   who retains all moral and economic rights under Spanish law
   (Royal Legislative Decree 1/1996) and applicable treaties.
   Publishing in a public repository is NOT a grant, license, waiver or
   dedication to the public domain. Anything not expressly permitted in
   section 4 is prohibited.

3. PURPOSE
   The Software is published solely so anyone can independently verify
   how it works, in particular what user data it does or does not
   collect, store or transmit. This license shall be construed
   restrictively in service of that purpose.

4. PERMITTED
   Subject to full compliance, anyone may, free of charge, on a
   non-exclusive, revocable and non-transferable basis:
   a) view and read the Software in this repository;
   b) download or clone it and run it in a private, isolated
      environment solely to audit its security, privacy or behavior,
      not accessible to third parties, for no longer than reasonably
      necessary, deleting copies afterwards;
   c) publish audit results with brief code quotations strictly needed
      to illustrate a finding, crediting this repository and Yovani
      Torres Favier, without enabling reconstruction of substantial
      parts and without misleading presentation;
   d) report bugs or vulnerabilities to the Author, preferably
      privately and with reasonable time to fix them;
   e) link to this repository or yamacoa.com.

5. PROHIBITED without the Author's prior express written consent,
   in whole or in part, directly or indirectly:
   5.1 Copying and distribution: copying or redistributing outside
       section 4; mirrors, public archives, packages or replicas;
       posting excerpts elsewhere beyond 4.c; selling, renting,
       sublicensing or transferring.
   5.2 Modification: modifying, adapting, translating or creating
       Derivative Works; porting; reimplementing its architecture or
       logic from the code to obtain a substantially similar product;
       removing or altering authorship notices or this license.
   5.3 Deployment and exploitation: deploying, hosting or making
       available the Software or any Derivative Work as a website, app,
       service, API, bot or agent, commercial or not; use in production,
       third-party-accessible staging, public demos or tests with real
       users; any commercial, consulting, training, fundraising, donation
       or grant purpose.
   5.4 Authorship: presenting any part as one's own or attributing its
       authorship, co-authorship, idea or development to anyone else;
       using it as one's own merit in portfolios, CVs, applications,
       contests, awards, grants or funding requests; claiming
       participation without the Author's written confirmation.
   5.5 Brand: using the Brand or the Author's name elsewhere;
       registering identical or confusingly similar domains, marks or
       accounts; suggesting endorsement or affiliation with any person,
       organization, party, movement, government or cause; impersonating
       Yamacoa or the Author.
   5.6 Content: scraping, bulk downloading, republishing, syndicating
       or aggregating Content; republishing whole or substantial parts
       even with credit; feeding other media or platforms; altering or
       decontextualizing Content to attribute views not expressed.
   5.7 Artificial intelligence: training, fine-tuning, distilling or
       evaluating AI models; inclusion in knowledge bases, vector
       indexes or RAG systems; providing it as context to an AI system
       to generate substantially similar code, text or products; text
       and data mining, which the Author expressly reserves under
       Article 4 of Directive (EU) 2019/790.
   5.8 Harmful use: surveillance, identification, profiling or
       persecution of people, or collecting user data without consent;
       disinformation, propaganda or unlawful content; attacking,
       overloading, exploiting or accessing yamacoa.com or its
       infrastructure without authorization.
   5.9 GitHub forks: a technical fork permitted by GitHub's Terms of
       Service grants none of the rights above; forks must keep this
       license intact and may not be modified, deployed or promoted.

